  "body": "## DO NOT MERGE \u2014 Bathcat existing-game remediation\n\n**Disposition:** `needs_followup`; OPEN + DRAFT + DO NOT MERGE. This is repaired audited-gap work, not completed canon.\n\n- Base: `e0e47b2f7593f5ee34c25c5695be9b6bed172afd`\n- Prior audited head (`REVISE`): `3b7eb962cf172f6adeb7dbf03dfafd14f972e0be`\n- Repaired exact head: `480ed343c3aa6fcfae48c88f63faddf54de5d2e9`\n- Branch: `kb/nemesis-lockdown-rules-components`\n- Target: BGG 310100, English 2022 first/release retail core box, Awaken Realms\n- Revision boundary: current Corebox Rulebook bytes are created 2021-08-06 / modified 2021-11-18; Room Sheet is dated 2021-08-06; FAQ is dated 2022-03-25. No first-retail printing marker or immutable release-era byte bridge was found, so all 12 target records remain `needs_followup`.\n\n## Exact four repairs on this head\n\n1. **Mars Surface branches:** split the compressed claim into operative Path/Crossroads/Area/Building movement; Area 3 and Technical-Corridor-effect exceptions; D12 normal, Danger, and Mars-card branches; Main Gate opening/irreversibility; and distinct alternate-side on-foot versus Rover Bunker routes. Mars Surface card-local effects remain UNKNOWN.\n2. **Encounter branches:** separated Intruder-token miniature/Surprise resolution from the Blank-token Noise/last-token Adult/return/end branch. Blank places no miniature and performs no Surprise comparison. Attack-card-local text remains UNKNOWN.\n3. **Weakness research:** recorded the first Weakness as discovered, retained Knowledge thresholds 3/5/8, limited discovery to once per Object type, added discard-without-reveal for reused types, and retained the 3-Knowledge gain. Weakness-card-local effects remain UNKNOWN.\n4. **FAQ denominator:** corrected the target-core page-2 denominator from eight to twelve Q&As and added the omitted Knee timing, computer-Room Action-card Power, Injury-dealing Items against Eggs, and multiple-Character Isolation rulings. No universal precedence doctrine was added; FAQ page-3 SG/Chytrid/Aftermath/Void Seeder/Medic/cross-game branches remain excluded.\n\n## Operative rules map\n\n- `rules/actions.okf.md`: Path/Crossroads connectivity and no-Noise Paths; every Crossroads-to-Area connection; Area 3 exception; Building/Exit Room entry; Surface Exploration before Noise; D12 1\u20134/Silence/Danger/Mars branches; Main Gate and Bunker eligibility; separate alternate-side on-foot and Rover routes; Intruder-token versus Blank-token Encounter resolution.\n- `rules/overview.okf.md`: first discovered Weakness; 3/5/8 thresholds; one discovery per Object type; reused-Object discard exception; 3 Knowledge per analysis.\n- `rules/edge-cases-faq.okf.md`: all twelve explicit target-core page-2 rulings with adjacent source triplets, bounded source roles, and page-3 exclusions.\n- `sources.okf.md`: twelve-Q&A source accounting and no-general-precedence boundary.\n\nOther acquired operative framework remains unchanged: setup and 68-row arithmetic; round/Event flow; Power/Light/Darkness; elevators and Technical Corridors; facility Fire/Malfunction/Doors; Contingency/Alert; CSS/Cargo; Venting and Autodestruction; objectives, escape, and victory.\n\n## Twelve explicit target-core FAQ rulings\n\n1. Queen bag conditional return.\n2. 15 Status markers.\n3. Items cannot affect another Character unless specified.\n4. Careful Movement still resolves revealed Danger.\n5. Archive differs from Alert.\n6. Repository resolves actor first, then other Characters in order.\n7. A CSS pod may launch repeatedly.\n8. Alert ending resolves like Time ending.\n9. Knee Serious Wound timing applies only to the first Movement Action on the first turn.\n10. An Action card merely requiring a computer Room does not inherently require Section Power unless specified.\n11. Items dealing Injuries may damage Eggs.\n12. Multiple Characters may lock into Isolation.\n\nThe FAQ controls only these twelve explicit target-core page-2 rulings. No broad card-versus-rulebook precedence rule was found. Later support repeats only 15-not-18 as current support.\n\n## Preserved closure and strict exclusions\n\n- Exact component arithmetic remains **68 printed rows / 682 listed physical units**: 23 card rows = 374, 6 miniature rows = 26, 39 other rows = 282 after Status 18\u219215; the printed typo total is 685.\n- Convention remains physical cards/tokens/miniatures once and each board/sheet/holder/bag/scanner/die once\u2014not faces/sides/surfaces/text, trays/inserts/multipart parts, or hidden identity denominators. No percentage/composite.\n- Current source/archive/support accounting, edition/exclusion/governing ledger, setup/round/endgame framework outside these patches, metadata/classification, reception/deckbuilder findings, and all visual bytes/manifest remain unchanged.\n- Excluded: crowdfunding/KS bundles, Stretch Goals, Chytrids, Untold Stories #3, Kings, terrain/Medic/cosmetics/add-ons/promos, original *Nemesis*, Aftermath, Void Seeders, Carnomorphs and compatibility law, translations, reprints without a bridge, and digital adaptation. Compatibility cards are physical inventory only.\n\n## Exact receipts\n\n- Corebox Rulebook: 6,075,325 bytes, 32 pages, SHA-256 `d8a939c54552e640b1d0efa1b7552a81e8b4205f04029634eb7f58d10ff2ef43`.\n- Room Sheet: 8,062,167 bytes, 4 pages, SHA-256 `6a88875bf52a04c681e373a8cceb8c676130ede505e1710ea5901494753294d4`.\n- FAQ: 678,267 bytes, 3 pages, SHA-256 `c5b9bf1297bb68bc2107d0591af3c2b81a24b75a816f42a889b1d467aff6648f`.\n- Downloads JSON: 317,363 bytes, SHA-256 `c9a25aef978e0348a279124c1d433c7921b7c7e2a80e24a3e9d45a321f7645b1`; exactly FAQ, Corebox Rulebook, Room Sheet, and separately labeled SG Rulebook in English.\n\n## Changed paths and gates\n\nRepair commit changes only:\n\n- `KnowledgeBase/BoardGames/games/nemesis-lockdown/rules/actions.okf.md`\n- `KnowledgeBase/BoardGames/games/nemesis-lockdown/rules/overview.okf.md`\n- `KnowledgeBase/BoardGames/games/nemesis-lockdown/rules/edge-cases-faq.okf.md`\n- `KnowledgeBase/BoardGames/games/nemesis-lockdown/sources.okf.md`\n- deterministic `TELEMETRY.md`\n\nGates on repaired committed head:\n\n- index generator completed; no semantic index delta\n- full OKF: **2619 files clean + INDEX fresh**\n- prescribed Node suite: **37 tests; 36 pass, 0 fail, 1 intentional skip**\n- committed-head intake gate: **clean**\n- base-to-head `git diff --check`: **clean**\n- exact-head GitHub `validate`: **SUCCESS**, run [`30636241368`](https://github.com/no-trbl-2-u/game-knowledge-base/actions/runs/30636241368), job [`91174449811`](https://github.com/no-trbl-2-u/game-knowledge-base/actions/runs/30636241368/job/91174449811), exact head `480ed343c3aa6fcfae48c88f63faddf54de5d2e9`\n\n## Exact residual help requested\n\n1. Confirmed English 2022 first-retail copy with SKU/UPC/lot/printing markers and nonreplacement physical faces/identities.\n2. Immutable first-retail rulebook/aid bytes or publisher bridge beyond the capture-truncated archive.\n3. Historical FAQ/support history beyond the complete current folder.\n4. Licensed hidden card/objective/Room/Contingency/token/die/board face/text denominators.\n\nBathcat-Authored: true\n\nReceiver: one wholly fresh Mennonite exact-head audit of `480ed343c3aa6fcfae48c88f63faddf54de5d2e9`; T remains final authority.\n\nNo approval, ready marking, promotion, or merge. **DO NOT MERGE.**\n",
